&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;The role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we continue to scale our business across EMEA, we are looking for an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Solutions Architecture Senior Manager, EMEA&lt;/strong&gt; to lead our customer-facing Solutions Architecture organization across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a leadership role responsible for building, developing and scaling a high-performing Solutions Architecture organization across multiple countries and markets. You will partner closely with EMEA Sales leadership, establish the operating model for the regional team, and ensure our Solutions Architects consistently deliver outstanding technical leadership and business value to customers. The scope of the role reflects where the business is today; as we scale, we expect the organization to specialize and subdivide, and this leader will help shape and staff that evolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced people leader who can build and empower strong teams while remaining close to customers, technology and our most strategic opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re welcome to work remotely from &lt;strong&gt;Europe&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead and coach a high-performing Solutions Architecture team across multiple countries and markets in EMEA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Solutions Architecture engagement model for EMEA in close partnership with regional Sales leadership, including how coverage and ownership are divided as the team expands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear priorities, operating mechanisms and performance expectations across the regional Solutions Architecture organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and scale the organization as the business grows, including hiring, coaching and developing senior technical professionals and future leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with CIOs, CTOs, Heads of Infrastructure, Heads of AI/ML, Business leaders and other senior stakeholders across strategic customers and partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion the voice of EMEA customers internally and provide guidance for Nebius&#39;s Product and Technology roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;We expect you to have:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven &lt;strong&gt;people-management experience&lt;/strong&gt;, including hiring, coaching and developing senior technical professionals and leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong track record of &lt;strong&gt;leading customer-facing technical teams across EMEA&lt;/strong&gt;, with experience managing teams distributed across multiple countries and markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building, scaling and operating regional Solutions Architecture, Sales Engineering, Customer Engineering or similar technical organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong &lt;strong&gt;player-coach mentality&lt;/strong&gt; with the ability to operate effectively at both leadership and execution levels — from organizational strategy and talent development to direct engagement in strategic customer opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the EMEA technology market and the ability to operate effectively across different countries, cultures, customer segments and levels of market maturity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively across both the &lt;strong&gt;technical and business dimensions&lt;/strong&gt; of complex customer engagements and influence C-level and senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent executive communication, presentation and stakeholder-management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in a fast-growing environment where team structures, coverage boundaries and scope of ownership will continue to evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Strong&quot;&gt;It will be an added bonus if you have:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of cloud-native infrastructure, including compute, storage, networking, security and Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership experience within a &lt;strong&gt;public cloud, hyperscaler or rapidly scaling cloud infrastructure organization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;GPU-based infrastructure workloads and accelerated computing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or supporting &lt;strong&gt;machine learning and AI workloads&lt;/strong&gt;, including training and inference&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of distributed AI/ML infrastructure and the compute, networking and storage considerations associated with large-scale GPU workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kubernetes-based AI/ML platforms, MLOps or AI infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience helping customers evaluate the economics of large-scale compute or GPU workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth and learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and innovative culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on impactful AI projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International environment and talented teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s it like to work at Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fast moving&amp;nbsp;- Bold thinking&amp;nbsp;- Constant growth&amp;nbsp;- Meaningful impact&amp;nbsp;- Trust and real ownership&amp;nbsp;- Opportunity to shape the future of AI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace and to providing equal employment opportunities in all aspects of employment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must be authorized to work in the country in which they apply and will be required to provide proof of employment eligibility as a condition of hire.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need accommodations during the application process, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Wolt and Roo operate under the DoorDash umbrella, and Customer Support sits at the intersection of brand experience, unit economics and long-term growth. This role owns the strategy on:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Where should we operate support, at what scale, and at what cost, across a rolling multi-year horizon?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How do we architect frontline service design to be AI-ready as frontline tooling evolves, deliver best-in-class customer experience, and remain cost-efficient?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;How do we manage our workforce with precision, eliminating waste, consolidating overlapping structures, and continuously improving headcount efficiency through automation and org redesign?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a permanent leadership role. The person in this seat will own network strategy, service design and workforce management as a continuous discipline, embedding deeply into Wolt, Roo and DoorDash technology stacks, building and refreshing the financial and operational case for change, and evolving the execution roadmap as the business, technology and market shift.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scope of Responsibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A. Support Service Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the demand and supply planning, and scheduling for the network, partnering deeply with upstream business owners and defect elimination to enable forecasting accuracy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own ongoing assessment of how service is structured and delivered at the frontline across both brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the role architecture map: what roles exist, what they do, where they overlap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate how tools (CRM, WFM, knowledge base, AI tools, ticketing) enable or constrain frontline roles, and keep this view current as tooling changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve the target-state frontline model aligned to AI-augmented ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously run gap analysis: current state vs. target state, with prioritised interventions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;B. Support Site Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the support site footprint across both brands as an ongoing portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and refresh strategic site scenarios across cost, quality, risk and scalability as conditions change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the financial model underpinning site strategy: OpEx, CapEx, transition cost, and planning cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously assess BPO vs. in-house mix, nearshore vs. offshore trade-offs, and consolidation opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring forward exec-ready recommendations as circumstances warrant, with clear pros, cons and decision criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the site strategy framed against contact volume reduction through automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;C. Workforce Management Transformation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own WFM maturity across both brands on an ongoing basis: demand forecasting, capacity planning, scheduling, real-time management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and close tooling gaps and duplication across Wolt and Roo WFM stacks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve the consolidated WFM target operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the continuous efficiency case, driven through:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Org consolidation:&amp;nbsp; merging duplicated WFM roles across the two brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contact automation: defect elimination and end-to-end customer-facing automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-assisted agent workflows: human-in-the-loop bot interfaces, AI-guided resolution, next-best-action tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scheduling and real-time optimisation via AI/ML tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own tooling requirements and vendor strategy (shortlists, entries, exits) as an ongoing responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;D. DoorDash Technology Integration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain deep, current working knowledge of DoorDash&#39;s support technology stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously translate technology capabilities into concrete business levers for the Wolt and Roo context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the dependency map between integration milestones and the Support transformation roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flag risks early where integration timelines could affect strategy execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;E. Execution Planning&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the rolling execution plan: prioritised initiatives, owners, investment, expected outcomes, refreshed as priorities shift.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the forward-looking roadmap: strategic bets, sequencing logic, capability-build requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own stakeholder alignment across Support Operations, Product, Finance and People functions on an ongoing basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Ongoing Responsibilities &amp;amp;&lt;/strong&gt; Outcomes&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Current state visibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain a living view of service design, site footprint, financial planning cycles and WFM maturity across Wolt &amp;amp; Roo, with an opinionated, forward-looking perspective on where the network needs to go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DoorDash technology translation:&lt;/strong&gt; Continuously map DoorDash technology capabilities to Wolt/Roo business levers, tracking upstream product, tooling and integration roadmaps and their implications for network design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support site strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain a multi-year scenario model with full financial analysis, pros &amp;amp; cons, and a standing recommended path, developed in partnership with the wider Strategy and Operations organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planning mechanisms:&lt;/strong&gt; Own and run weekly, monthly, quarterly and annual mechanisms for demand and supply planning (long and short term) and scheduling/real-time management, optimising for customer experience and efficiency, with clear visibility for executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WFM transformation:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the consolidated operating model, tooling spec, and the efficiency case for the organisation, with signed-off financial projections refreshed as the business evolves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Roadmap ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain a rolling forward roadmap covering strategic sequencing, capability investments, and automation maturity milestones, ratified through regular leadership review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Keep all key workstream owners briefed, committed and clear on accountabilities on an ongoing basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All recommendations must be underpinned by a financial model, and must be decision-ready on first presentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operating Rhythm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
